    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup features a clear tier of elite production led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), whose aggressive presence on the basepaths against the right-handed Pallante is our most potent asset for the scarcity-heavy stolen base category. **Yordan Alvarez** (73.90) and **Junior Caminero** (73.43) provide the requisite power-hitting anchors, with **Yordan Alvarez** benefiting from an elite xwOBA profile and **Junior Caminero** capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Ure\u00f1a. **Kazuma Okamoto** (67.98) also warrants a strong recommendation; his score is significantly elevated by a +16% park factor adjustment, making him our most efficient third-base option for today\u2019s slate. We are tracking the effectiveness of **Christian Yelich** (65.69) closely as well, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Teng keeps his floor high in a day where maximizing counting stats is critical.\n\nThe optimization process required a difficult decision regarding the bench, ultimately leaving **Carson Benge** (48.18) on the outside looking in. While **Carson Benge** benefits from a strong lead-off spot, his efficiency score was dampened by a suboptimal matchup against the resilient Meyer and negative park factors, causing him to fall just short of the thresholds set by **Caleb Durbin** and **Luke Raley**. We are proceeding with **Trea Turner** (59.12) and **Kyle Schwarber** (57.48) despite the challenging 3.49 xERA of Wrobleski; both remain startable due to high volume, though we recognize the elevated risk in these specific matchups. **Colt Keith** and **Lars Nootbaar** remain unavailable due to lineup status and injury, respectively, and we continue to monitor the minor league progress of **Hyeseong Kim** for potential late-season roster depth.",
